# ============================================================================
# DebateKit Web — Local Development Secrets
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS:
#   Runtime secrets for the web app's SSR worker (`debatekit-web`,
#   TanStack Start on Cloudflare Workers). Wrangler loads `.dev.vars`
#   automatically during `wrangler dev` and exposes them as `env.*`.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#   Then fill in real values. `.dev.vars` is gitignored.
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   The web app currently has NO required server-side secrets — all auth,
#   AI calls, payments, etc. happen via the API worker (apps/api) and the
#   browser hits it directly with credentialed fetches.
#
#   Public, browser-exposed config (PostHog client key, maintenance flag,
#   env label) is committed in apps/web/.env / .env.preview / .env.production
#   as `VITE_*` vars, statically replaced by Vite at build time.
#
#   This file exists for future server-only secrets (e.g. a server-side
#   PostHog feature-flag personal key, an SSR-only third-party API). Add
#   them here as needed and run `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <env>`
#   for deployed envs.
#
# DEPLOYING:
#   For preview/production:
#     wrangler secret put <NAME> --env preview
#     wrangler secret put <NAME> --env production
# ============================================================================


# ============================================================================
# (no required secrets yet — add SSR-only secrets here as the app grows)
# ============================================================================

# Example (uncomment and rename when adding a secret):
# MY_SERVER_ONLY_API_KEY=<get-from-service-console>
